    "question": "Miggy's mom brought home 3 bags of birthday hats. Each bag has 15 hats. Miggy accidentally tore off 5 hats. During the party, only 25 hats were used. How many hats were unused?",
    "gold": "15",
    "answer": "There are a total of 15 x 3 = <<15*3=45>>45 hats in 3 bags.\nSince 5 tore off, only 45 - 5 = <<45-5=40>>40 hats were left.\nThus, 40 - 25 = <<40-25=15>>15 hats were unused.\n#### 15"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the number of unused hats, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of hats Miggy's mom brought home.\n2. Subtract the number of hats that were torn off by Miggy.\n3. Subtract the number of hats that were used during the party.\n4. The result will be the number of unused hats.\n\nLet's go through each step in detail:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of hats:\n   Miggy's mom brought home 3 bags of hats, and each bag contains 15 hats.\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 15 = 45\n   \\]\n   So, the total number of hats is 45.\n\n2. Subtract the number of hats that were torn off:\n   Miggy tore off 5 hats.\n   \\[\n   45 - 5 = 40\n   \\]\n   So, after Miggy tore off the hats, there are 40 hats left.\n\n3. Subtract the number of hats that were used:\n   During the party, 25 hats were used.\n   \\[\n   40 - 25 = 15\n   \\]\n   So, the number of unused hats is 15.\n\nTherefore, the number of unused hats is \\boxed{15}.",
